,"    optOutTrackingByDefault: true",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SDK applies most calls later, on its own serial queue, while checking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the opt-out flag on the caller’s thread. The adapter papers over the gaps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that leaves: consent changes take effect before their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"type":"text","text":" call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":" drains the whole queue, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reset()"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps both queued"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events and a withdrawn consent, and opting out deletes the queue instead"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of leaving it to be sent later."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The struct is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@unchecked Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance"},{"type":"text","text":" serializes its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracking work on internal queues, and every copy of the service shares one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SDK instance. The exceptions are the diagnostic setters, which write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unsynchronized SDK properties — set those once, at launch."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/15SwiduxAnalytics0B7ServiceP","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"